  /* Trust metrics), plus a small revealed description. The dark layer     */
  /* lives on ::before (opacity 0→1) rather than swapping the card's own   */
  /* background-image directly — background-image itself doesn't          */
  /* transition smoothly, only opacity/color do, so this is what gives     */
  /* the fade-to-dark its actual animation; the moving-highlight layer     */
  /* reuses the sitewide @keyframes hero-sheen (global.css) rather than    */
  /* a one-off animation, so the motion reads as the same "alive" gradient */
  /* as the rest of the site. `.friction-card`'s own transition list       */
  /* below deliberately REPEATS [data-flow-fade]'s opacity/transform       */
  /* transition (same selector specificity, this rule loads later so it    */
  /* would otherwise silently replace — not merge with — that one and      */
  /* kill the scroll-in/out fade) alongside the border-color transition    */
  /* this component actually adds. */
  .friction-card {
